{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1881","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1881","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1881\",\"parent_revision\":\"eb7521babcad5c12586c87ccb558bb651ac2d259\",\"root_revision\":\"77475e1a619f8dde1309d682320072b277b160646778ab7e43e528b6b641d984\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `_build_compact_manifest` function location | DERIVABLE | Grep `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/` |\\n| 2 | `BacklogViewResult` model fields | DERIVABLE | Check backlog_core models |\\n| 3 | Fix commit `2cccb78` merged in PR #1871 | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information available or derivable.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **test: add regression test for backlog_view issue_number null when result.issue is empty** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Copilot review on PR #1871 (2026-04-22)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Bug (regression test). Low complexity. Additive test only. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Test calls `_build_compact_manifest` (or `backlog_view` via fixture) with a `BacklogViewResult` where `result.issue == ''` and `result.number` is set to an integer\\n- Assertion: `compact_manifest['issue_number']` equals `result.number` (not `null`)\\n- Test named `test_compact_manifest_issue_number_from_result_number_when_issue_empty` or similar\\n- Test placed in existing backlog_view test file or `test_backlog_core_compact.py`\\n- References commit `2cccb78` and bug fix PR #1871 in test docstring for traceability\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 add regression test in appropriate test file\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a backlog_core developer, I need a regression test covering the scenario where `backlog_view` is called with a pure issue selector and the item has no local `**Issue**` link but `result.number` IS populated by backend enrichment, so the original `issue_number: null` bug cannot silently regress.\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCopilot review comment on PR #1871: https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/pull/1871#discussion_r3121080140\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe fix in #1871 (commit 2cccb78) changed `_build_compact_manifest` to use `result.number` as the primary source for `issue_number` in the compact summary, falling back to parsing `result.issue` only when `result.number` is None.\\n\\nHowever, no regression test was added for the specific failure scenario: when `backlog_view` is called with a pure issue selector (e.g. `\\\"#1859\\\"`) and the item has no local `**Issue**: #N` link (`result.issue == \\\"\\\"`), but `result.number` IS populated by backend enrichment.\\n\\nWithout this test, the original bug (`issue_number: null`) could silently regress.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA test in `plugins/development-harness/tests/` (or the existing backlog server test suite) that:\\n1. Constructs a `ViewItemResult` with `issue=\\\"\\\"` and `number=1859`\\n2. Calls `_build_compact_manifest` (or the full `backlog_view` summary path)\\n3. Asserts that the returned dict contains `issue_number: 1859` (not `null` or `None`)\\n\\nOptionally also test the fallback path: `issue=\\\"#1859\\\"`, `number=None` \u2192 `issue_number: 1859` (parsed from string).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e33724df83d84f5ad4d720092478a2dfb67c75969ba8d88fd8c3d1c7cea82b40\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPulJ8A\"}"}